id=a52sxq_adreno_driver
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Adreno GPU driver selector (V@0530 stock default, V@0849 / V@0863 selectable)
author=kusti420
description=The A14 vendor ships the Adreno 642L userspace driver V@0530 (11/22/21), which stays in /vendor untouched and is the default (testers asked for it back). Two newer builds of Qualcomm's LA.VENDOR.14.3.4.11 branch are shipped as complete 64-bit sets under /vendor/k4gpu: V@0849.0 (09/19/25, community module by @sudami) and V@0863.1 (12/24/25, "Adreno GPU Driver 863.1" module by @Joshaby), each with its a660 SQE microcode. Settings > K4_UN1CA > UI > GPU driver writes persist.sys.k4.gpu_driver; /system/etc/init/k4_gpu_driver.rc overlays the selected set over /vendor/lib64 at early-boot (before the first /dev/kgsl-3d0 open, which loads the microcode), binds its microcode and the Vulkan 1.3 feature file (V@0530 reports Vulkan 1.1, the newer builds 1.3), and reports sys.k4.gpu_active. A boot with a newly selected driver that never reaches boot_completed falls back to V@0530 on the next boot (persist.sys.k4.gpu_trial / gpu_failed). Benchmarks 2026-10-20 (3DMark, same start temperatures): V@0849 +5% GL / +8% Vulkan graphics, same clocks and heat, 0 GPU faults on both. The 32-bit V@0530 libs stay (no 32-bit process uses the GPU).
